T52 PositiveSampleMean development history

attempt-01-independent-core.log
  Initial elaboration exposed four concrete API issues: the definition had to
  be unfolded before measurability/rewrite steps; `MemLp` finite sums use
  `memLp_finsetSum'`; and the final constant sum required the cardinality of
  `Fin n` to be normalized explicitly.

attempt-02-independent-core.log
  The remaining normalization goal contained `Finset.univ.card`; added
  `Finset.card_univ` and replaced the deprecated integral theorem name.

attempt-03-independent-core.log
  `field_simp` had already closed the normalization goal, leaving an extra
  `ring`; removed the redundant tactic.

attempt-04-independent-core.log
  Independent variance core passed.  Renamed the mathematically redundant
  explicit `A >= 0` binder with an underscore prefix to silence its linter;
  the contract assumption remains in the theorem type.

attempt-05-rpow-helpers.log
  Replaced an unsuitable positivity call with `sq_nonneg`; reassociated the
  exponential product before applying `Real.exp_add`.

attempt-06-rpow-helpers.log
  Real-rpow ratio and exact horizon-scaling identity passed.

attempt-07-scaled-budget.log
  Positive-mean budget branch passed.  The zero-mean branch required its
  integral to be normalized from `(mhat - 0)^2` to `mhat^2`.

attempt-08-scaled-budget.log
  Normalized the target as well as the stored zero-integral identity.

attempt-09-combined-risk.log
  Full source, including the frozen T51 import and exact `25/1024` risk
  composition, passed with no output.

Final verification
  `build.log`: fresh Lake target build, 3457/3457 jobs.
  `axioms.log`: every authored export uses only propext, Classical.choice,
  and Quot.sound.
  `source-scan.log`: empty sorry/admit/axiom/opaque scan.
